'' =====================================================================
'' conflict-testM-bitmap-sparse.spin2  --  settles H-4 (BITMAP SPARSE: the
''   user-facing word) and confirms the DOTSIZE >= 4 gate
''
'' QUESTION 1 (the WORD):  our own docs disagree about what SPARSE looks like.
''     ch04:49  + bitmap.yaml:32 : "OUTLINE each magnified pixel / grid-BORDER color"
''     ch04:398 + the example     : "round dot against its BACKGROUND"
''     v55 L1331                  : "large ROUND pixels against a COLORED BACKGROUND"
''     REF BITMAP_ToO             : "NOT a border/frame -- a SOLID FILL of the whole
''                                   cell, with a round dot in the pixel's own color
''                                   drawn on top"
''   The mechanism is settled; the WORD WE SHOW THE READER is not, and there is no
''   BITMAP entry in the empirical ledger.  Figure and ground are inverted between
''   two passages of the SAME chapter.  A picture ends it.
''
'' QUESTION 2 (the GATE):  SetSize self-disables SPARSE unless DOTSIZE >= 4 on BOTH
''   axes.  Ratified from source, never seen.  If real, the DOTSIZE-3 rail below
''   shows NO sparse color at all.
''
'' TWO-RAIL DESIGN (three rails, actually):
''   RAIL-OFF  (known-false): DOTSIZE 12, NO SPARSE  -> solid GREEN blocks, NO RED
''                            anywhere.  Proves red only ever comes from SPARSE.
''   RAIL-GATE (known-false): DOTSIZE 3, SPARSE RED  -> gate FAILS (3 < 4), so SPARSE
''                            self-disables -> again NO RED.  Proves the gate.
''   REAL CASE (the question): DOTSIZE 12, SPARSE RED -> where does the RED go?
''   If RAIL-OFF and the REAL CASE look the same, the sampler cannot discriminate
''   -> INCONCLUSIVE (we know it), never a false positive.
''
'' COLOR CHOICE: every pixel fed is pure GREEN $00FF00; SPARSE is pure RED $FF0000.
''   Maximum separation, and it makes the read a simple question about WHERE the red
''   is -- not a judgement call about shape vocabulary:
''     red forms a SOLID SQUARE CELL behind a round green dot  -> "background" (v55/ToO)
''     red forms only a THIN OUTLINE around a green square      -> "border/grid" (ch04:49)
''
'' *** SAVE WINDOW IS MANDATORY HERE -- DO NOT "SIMPLIFY" IT TO SAVE ***
''   A non-WINDOW BITMAP SAVE writes the bitmap at 1x, UN-DOTSIZEd: it would hand
''   back the 6x4 source pixels and tell us NOTHING about the magnified rendering,
''   which is the entire question.  SAVE WINDOW scrapes the on-screen window.
''   Consequence: SAVE WINDOW is a DESKTOP scrape and is OCCLUSION-VULNERABLE --
''   keep these three windows unobscured while the program runs.
''
'' OTHER SAVE-TRAP COMPLIANCE: filename present and LAST; nothing follows SAVE
''   (a trailing keyword is consumed and discarded); no UPDATE mode (SAVE writes
''   the FRONT buffer and would capture a stale frame).
'' =====================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 100_000_000

PUB main() | i

  ' 6 x 4 canvas so the cell structure is large and unmistakable when magnified
  debug(`BITMAP SpOff  SIZE 6 4 DOTSIZE 12 RGB24)                     ' RAIL-OFF
  debug(`BITMAP SpGate SIZE 6 4 DOTSIZE 3  RGB24 SPARSE $FF0000)      ' RAIL-GATE (3 < 4)
  debug(`BITMAP SpOn   SIZE 6 4 DOTSIZE 12 RGB24 SPARSE $FF0000)      ' REAL CASE

  ' every pixel pure GREEN -- so ANY red on screen can only have come from SPARSE
  repeat i from 0 to 23
    debug(`SpOff  `($00FF00))
    debug(`SpGate `($00FF00))
    debug(`SpOn   `($00FF00))

  waitms(400)

  ' SAVE WINDOW -- see the banner above.  Filename LAST, nothing after it.
  debug(`SpOff  save window 'sparseM_off')
  debug(`SpGate save window 'sparseM_gate3')
  debug(`SpOn   save window 'sparseM_on12')

  waitms(500)
  repeat
